1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:08,483
GTA 6 has been out for a week, and on the most powerful PlayStation you can buy, it runs at 30 frames a second.

2
00:00:08,763 --> 00:00:11,345
The PC version isn't even announced yet.

3
00:00:11,625 --> 00:00:16,436
But the console version already tells us a lot about what a PC will need.

4
00:00:16,716 --> 00:00:22,347
By the end, you'll know whether your PC is in the running, and which upgrade actually matters.

5
00:00:24,097 --> 00:00:28,116
Here's what we know as of late November 2026.

6
00:00:28,396 --> 00:00:34,964
GTA 6 launched on November 19th for PS5 and Xbox Series consoles.

7
00:00:35,244 --> 00:00:45,027
Digital Foundry found a 30 frame cap on both PS5 models, with an internal resolution around 1440p.

8
00:00:45,307 --> 00:00:51,559
The PS5 Pro upscales that to something close to 4K, and it holds 30 more steadily.

9
00:00:51,839 --> 00:00:55,349
The base PS5 dips below 30 in big fights.

10
00:00:55,629 --> 00:00:57,753
And there's no performance mode at all.

11
00:00:58,503 --> 00:01:00,141
So when does it reach PC?

12
00:01:00,421 --> 00:01:01,792
Rockstar hasn't said.

13
00:01:02,072 --> 00:01:12,223
In October, GamesBeat reported, citing four unnamed sources, that a PC version is planned for the first quarter of 2027.

14
00:01:12,503 --> 00:01:13,987
Rockstar didn't comment.

15
00:01:14,267 --> 00:01:24,471
For context, GTA 5 reached PC about a year and a half after it first launched on consoles, and Red Dead Redemption 2 took about a year.

16
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:26,617
Either way, you have time to plan.

17
00:01:27,367 --> 00:01:31,175
Now let's open the console, because it's basically a PC.

18
00:01:31,455 --> 00:01:48,268
The PS5 has eight Zen 2 processor cores running at up to 3.5 gigahertz, a graphics chip rated at about 10 teraflops, 16 gigabytes of memory shared between the game and the graphics, and a fast NVMe SSD.

19
00:01:48,548 --> 00:01:57,883
In Digital Foundry's tests, its graphics power lands close to an RTX 20 70 Super or a Radeon RX 67 hundred.

20
00:01:58,163 --> 00:02:04,819
Its processor is a lot like a Ryzen 7 37 hundred X, with lower clocks and less cache.

21
00:02:05,569 --> 00:02:13,769
Quick favor before we go further: over 99 percent of the watch time on this channel comes from people who aren't subscribed.

22
00:02:14,049 --> 00:02:20,149
If this helps you plan your upgrade, subscribing is free, and it tells me to keep making these.

23
00:02:20,899 --> 00:02:22,672
So why only 30 frames?

24
00:02:22,952 --> 00:02:26,216
Because the processor is the wall, not the graphics chip.

25
00:02:26,496 --> 00:02:35,218
Every pedestrian, every car, every bit of traffic and physics is worked out by the CPU before the GPU can draw the frame.

26
00:02:35,498 --> 00:02:40,271
At 30 frames a second, the CPU has 33 milliseconds per frame.

27
00:02:40,551 --> 00:02:43,073
At 60, it gets just 16 and a half.

28
00:02:43,353 --> 00:02:49,557
Digital Foundry has said GTA 6's dense crowds are what keep the consoles at 30.

29
00:02:50,307 --> 00:02:52,076
The PS5 Pro proves it.

30
00:02:52,356 --> 00:03:02,423
Sony gave it a much bigger graphics chip, but the processor only got about 10 percent faster, from 3.5 to 3.85 gigahertz.

31
00:03:02,703 --> 00:03:06,682
The result is a sharper image and a steadier 30, not 60.

32
00:03:06,962 --> 00:03:10,600
More graphics power alone doesn't buy frames in this game.

33
00:03:11,350 --> 00:03:14,518
You can check your own processor in about 30 seconds.

34
00:03:14,798 --> 00:03:19,375
On Windows, open Task Manager, go to Performance, and click CPU.

35
00:03:19,655 --> 00:03:25,579
The name of your processor is in the top right, and below the graph you'll see how many cores it has.

36
00:03:25,859 --> 00:03:29,427
Search that name with the word launch, and you'll know its age.

37
00:03:29,707 --> 00:03:40,809
An eight-core chip from 2022 or later is in a very different league from a four-core chip from 2017, even if the gigahertz number looks similar.

38
00:03:41,559 --> 00:03:46,809
That makes the CPU the most important part for GTA 6 on PC.

39
00:03:47,089 --> 00:03:51,798
To hold 60, a processor has to do the console's work in half the time.

40
00:03:52,078 --> 00:04:01,732
Digital Foundry's Oliver Mackenzie has warned that even twice the console's performance may not hold 60 in the most CPU-heavy scenes.

41
00:04:02,012 --> 00:04:16,188
Modern eight-core chips with large caches are far ahead of the console's Zen 2 cores, but older four- and six-core processors from 2019 and earlier will probably land near console frame rates.

42
00:04:16,938 --> 00:04:19,654
The graphics card matters less than you'd think.

43
00:04:19,934 --> 00:04:33,176
Matching the console's look, 1440p internally at 30 frames, should only take a card in the RTX 20 70 Super or RX 67 hundred class.

44
00:04:33,456 --> 00:04:42,023
Doubling the frame rate at the same settings needs roughly double that, which is today's mid-range, especially with upscaling turned on.

45
00:04:42,303 --> 00:04:46,617
That's my estimate until Rockstar publishes real requirements.

46
00:04:47,367 --> 00:04:50,525
Upscaling helps, but only with half of the problem.

47
00:04:50,805 --> 00:05:02,634
DLSS, FSR and XeSS render the game at a lower resolution and rebuild a sharp image, which is exactly what the PS5 Pro does with PSSR.

48
00:05:02,914 --> 00:05:04,684
That frees up the graphics card.

49
00:05:04,964 --> 00:05:14,923
But if the processor is already the wall, rendering fewer pixels changes nothing, because the CPU still has to simulate the whole city every frame.

50
00:05:15,203 --> 00:05:23,241
Frame generation can make the counter read 60, but the game still reacts to your input at the real frame rate underneath.

51
00:05:23,991 --> 00:05:26,196
Memory is where PCs differ most.

52
00:05:26,476 --> 00:05:30,816
A console shares its 16 gigabytes between the game and the graphics.

53
00:05:31,096 --> 00:05:36,496
A PC splits them: system RAM for the game, video memory on the card.

54
00:05:36,776 --> 00:05:46,427
An eight gigabyte card is the most likely to need lower texture settings in a game this detailed, so 12 or 16 gigabytes is the safer bet.

55
00:05:46,707 --> 00:05:51,923
For system memory, 16 gigabytes is the floor, and 32 is comfortable.

56
00:05:52,203 --> 00:05:57,597
And plan on an NVMe SSD with plenty of free space, not a hard drive.

57
00:05:58,347 --> 00:06:01,980
Memory is also the most expensive part to buy right now.

58
00:06:02,260 --> 00:06:05,812
The AI boom has pushed memory prices way up this year.

59
00:06:06,092 --> 00:06:20,812
In mid-November, a 32 gigabyte DDR5 kit was listed at around 430 to 600 dollars in the US, and graphics cards with lots of video memory cost more than they did at launch.

60
00:06:21,092 --> 00:06:25,559
That's one more reason not to rush an upgrade for a game you can't buy yet.

61
00:06:26,309 --> 00:06:27,791
So should you upgrade now?

62
00:06:28,071 --> 00:06:28,618
No.

63
00:06:28,898 --> 00:06:36,960
There are no official specs, memory and graphics card prices are high this year, and the PC version is likely months away.

64
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:44,856
Rockstar usually publishes system requirements close to a PC launch, and prices could look very different by then.

65
00:06:45,606 --> 00:06:51,673
Here's how that plays out on three example PCs, and these are estimates, not benchmarks.

66
00:06:51,953 --> 00:07:05,914
A PC with a six-core processor from 2019 and an RTX 20 70 Super will probably look and run a lot like the PS5: around 30 frames, with dips in crowded streets.

67
00:07:06,194 --> 00:07:18,279
A PC with a recent eight-core chip and a 16 gigabyte mid-range card should get well above the console, likely near 60 in most areas, with dips in the busiest scenes.

68
00:07:18,559 --> 00:07:27,136
And a high-end PC with a large-cache gaming processor has the best chance of holding 60, but even it may not be locked there.

69
00:07:27,886 --> 00:07:29,070
Here's the verdict.

70
00:07:29,350 --> 00:07:30,993
Check your processor first.

71
00:07:31,273 --> 00:07:37,710
If it's an eight-core chip from the last few years, you're probably in good shape, and the rest is settings.

72
00:07:37,990 --> 00:07:45,950
If it's a four- or six-core chip from 2019 or earlier, that's the upgrade to plan for, before the graphics card.

73
00:07:46,230 --> 00:07:50,576
And if your card has 8 gigabytes, expect to turn textures down.

74
00:07:51,326 --> 00:08:00,857
Next up, on Wednesday: DDR4 or DDR5 in 2026, and why this year's memory prices changed the answer.

75
00:08:01,137 --> 00:08:12,509
If this helped, share it with a friend who's waiting for GTA 6 on PC, subscribe for new verdicts every Monday, Wednesday and Friday, and comment your questions below.

